{"author":{"id":"f4f7e123ea38957901744390924e1710825e6d55b5113472173231f66fb2d926"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793957342,"nonce":"Iz3ZG8AsfB4wdosi3YgV47AnE/g=","title":"Continuation audit on 2026-11-06 at source b60305d67234d574f9d66c5f7144861d78a75079 found two related IF/ELSE compiler failures missed by the release QA matrix. A fresh cmake --build build -j 2 completed before the confirming probes.","message":"1. Valid numeric THEN/ELSE silently takes the wrong path:\n10 X=0\n20 IF X THEN 50 ELSE 60\n30 PRINT \"FALLTHROUGH\":END\n50 PRINT \"THEN\":END\n60 PRINT \"ELSE\":END\n\nInterpreter: ELSE. Compiled: FALLTHROUGH.\n\n2. Numeric ELSE to an undefined line after a statement THEN:\n10 ON ERROR GOTO 100\n20 X=0\n30 IF X THEN PRINT \"THEN\" ELSE 999\n40 END\n100 PRINT ERR;ERL\n\nInterpreter: error 8 at line 30, caught by the handler. Generated C: gcc rejects label L_999 used but not defined. With a numeric THEN target instead, the same missing ELSE target is silently ignored and the handler is never called.\n\nAll three confirming cases reproduced at -O0, -O1, -O2, -O3, -O2 --inline-arrays and -O2 --safe (18 failed comparisons). Ordinary unmatched NEXT and unconditional DEFINT delegation probes passed at -O0/-O2; those older findings should not be reopened based only on stale bot comments.\n\nSuspected sites: src/codegen.c IF emission checks TOK_ELSE immediately after reading the numeric THEN target without accounting for remaining separators; src/analysis.c target collection handles THEN but not ELSE. Inspect exact token layout before fixing. Preserve nested IF/ELSE binding and assignment analysis. Add taken/untaken valid and undefined ELSE regressions, including ON ERROR / ERR / ERL behavior, across supported modes.\n\nTreat these as release follow-up before merging PR #7 and publishing v0.18.1. Rebuild and verify the draft archives against the corrected commit after tests pass. The current published release is v0.18.0; v0.18.1 remains a draft at b60305d.\n\nEvidence: /home/evaletov/.local/share/gwbasic-2026/reviews/2026-11-06-priority-refresh/else-audit.json and adjacent .bas/.c files. The numeric ELSE target-collection issue was mentioned in the earlier CodeRabbit review body of https://github.com/evvaletov/gw-basic-2026/pull/7; no new bot review has completed on b60305d.","files":null}]}